    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c11d2346d6c74eff9e75fc9006507278",
      "statement": "The current entrypoint treats the model-memory estimate as a warning guard rather than an unconditional abort: it catches `RuntimeError` from estimation or `assert_fits_in_available_gpu`, prints a memory warning, and continues, while the GPU assertion itself is a no-op on CPU.",
